WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000 line:0% align:end size:15%
<ruby><rt>kaa.lt</rt></ruby>

1
00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:15.580
This place is totally infested with Undead!

2
00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:17.750
We're close to the dungeon.

3
00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:19.500
Hey, Jean!

4
00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:20.200
Hm?

5
00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:25.540
Can we have dibs on the crystals from these monsters?
Take it outta our pay if you have to.

6
00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:28.660
That's fine. What are you going to use them for?

7
00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:30.290
Uh, well, y'know...

8
00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:31.700
Soulsight!

9
00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:34.830
Ah, I see. It's one of your stat values.

10
00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:40.450
You get stronger by absorbing
a certain number of crystals, I'm guessing.

11
00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:44.120
Man, your unique skill is a pain in the butt.
You see through everything.

12
00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:44.870
Mm-hmm.

13
00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:49.330
I must say, I've never heard of anyone
with a crystal stat like that before.

14
00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:53.200
Does it allow you to obtain skills, by chance?

15
00:00:53.330 --> 00:00:54.410
Uh-oh!

16
00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:56.450
Seems I've hit the nail on the head.

17
00:00:58.120 --> 00:00:59.250
Just my genius at work!

18
00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:02.250
That's crazy, how did you figure it out?

19
00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:04.910
Because the skills you possess are far from the norm.

20
00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:08.120
I noticed a few that only monsters should have.

21
00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:10.870
Soulsight is a force to be reckoned with.

22
00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:16.870
That reminds me, I once encountered a monster in
this dungeon with a skill that messed with my Soulsight.

23
00:01:17.290 --> 00:01:19.410
You did? No way!

24
00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:22.000
Wow! I want that skill!

25
00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:25.500
I'll tell you more about it later. We're here.

26
00:01:26.370 --> 00:01:30.790
Now let us venture into the sky island dungeon!

27
00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:08.370
Such animus in the air. How nostalgic.

28
00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:09.370
EPISODE 2:

29
00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:09.370
JEAN DU VIX KNOWS HIS STUFF

30
00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:09.910
What's animus?

31
00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:13.200
The regretful feelings of the dead.
They cling to their past life and refuse to die.

32
00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:19.790
Whenever crystals get infused with animus, they create
powerful undead monsters known as vengeful spirits.

33
00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:21.830
Andy was one of those.

34
00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:24.200
He was?

35
00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:27.790
Necromancers such as myself
can make use of those powerful spirits

36
00:03:27.790 --> 00:03:30.290
and connect with their souls to purify them.

37
00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:35.290
It can be considered a form of salvation,
since they are bound by their own hatred.

38
00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:40.000
However... this place is like none I've ever seen.

39
00:03:40.580 --> 00:03:45.540
The depth of pained animus that runs through here
surpasses any normal dungeon.

40
00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:49.080
Sounds like we're walking into big trouble, then.

41
00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:50.620
Anything we should watch out for?

42
00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:53.410
I shall lead the way and disarm the traps.

43
00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:56.500
You two just focus on fighting the monsters.

44
00:03:57.450 --> 00:03:58.700
Okie-dokie.

45
00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:02.500
SKY ISLAND DUNGEON

46
00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:02.500
B1F

47
00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:07.620
Hey, Jean. Can you tell us more about
the skill you said messed with your Soulsight?

48
00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:12.080
Sure. Down on the second floor
there is an undead monster called a Mimic

49
00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:14.620
with a skill known as "Identify Jammer."

50
00:04:14.910 --> 00:04:18.660
Identify Jammer? That doesn't seem
as good as my Identify Protection.

51
00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:20.250
Well, let me finish.

52
00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:24.330
There is a special rare species
of that monster known as a "Counterfeit,"

53
00:04:21.450 --> 00:04:24.370
MIMIC

54
00:04:21.450 --> 00:04:24.370
THREAT RANK: E

55
00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:29.000
which has a unique skill called "Fake Identity."

56
00:04:25.750 --> 00:04:29.370
COUNTERFEIT

57
00:04:25.750 --> 00:04:29.370
THREAT RANK: D

58
00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:35.500
It gives them the ability to display fake stats,
as opposed to blocking Identify.

59
00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:38.120
Ah, to lure people into a false sense of security?

60
00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:40.910
Real

61
00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:40.910
Level: High

62
00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:40.910
Name: Fran

63
00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:40.910
Black Cat

64
00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:40.910
Equipped: Teacher

65
00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:40.910
Black Cat Set

66
00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:40.910
Skills:

67
00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:40.910
A bunch of good ones

68
00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:40.910
Jamming

69
00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:40.910
Weary

70
00:04:38.450 --> 00:04:39.910
That skill would make the perfect combination

71
00:04:39.910 --> 00:04:41.080
with Identify Protection,

72
00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:48.700
Name: Fluffy

73
00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:48.700
Fake

74
00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:48.700
Level: Low

75
00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:48.700
Fluffball

76
00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:48.700
Equipped: Stick

77
00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:48.700
Leaves

78
00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:48.700
Skills:

79
00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:48.700
Loves curry

80
00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:48.700
Falsified

81
00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:48.700
Fooled

82
00:04:41.290 --> 00:04:43.250
since you could fully deceive an enemy

83
00:04:43.250 --> 00:04:46.750
with the fake stats by blocking off your real ones.

84
00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:48.540
Wow! That's awesome!

85
00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:51.500
And it even works on your Soulsight?

86
00:04:51.790 --> 00:04:53.790
Indeed, I experienced it firsthand.

87
00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:56.450
It should prove effective against
other types of magic vision, as well.

88
00:04:57.250 --> 00:04:59.330
I wanna get the Fake Identity skill!

89
00:04:59.330 --> 00:05:01.370
Yeah! It sounds like a must have!

90
00:05:01.370 --> 00:05:02.830
Raring to go now, are we?

91
00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:04.160
Totally!

92
00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:05.410
Let's get moving!

93
00:05:06.830 --> 00:05:07.870
Ah, wait a moment!

94
00:05:08.830 --> 00:05:09.500
Oh crap!

95
00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:14.790
The path ahead is laden with a plethora of deadly traps.

96
00:05:14.950 --> 00:05:16.370
Trope box ticked.

97
00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:20.870
Fran, could you bring Summon Sphere #1
out of storage for me?

98
00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:24.290
Oh, that stuff you had us keep in our pocket dimension?

99
00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:30.500
Instant Summon! High Undead!

100
00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:33.870
Thy name is Selkan!

101
00:05:34.830 --> 00:05:40.870
This an undead servant of mine who I customized
with my necromancy skills especially for this expedition.

102
00:05:37.950 --> 00:05:41.450
SELKAN

103
00:05:37.950 --> 00:05:41.450
(CUSTOM REVENANT)

104
00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:41.450
RACE: UNDEAD MONSTER

105
00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:41.450
STATUS: CONTRACT, UNDEAD

106
00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:41.450
VIT:

107
00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:41.450
INT:

108
00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:41.450
STR:

109
00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:41.450
AGI:

110
00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:41.450
SKILLS:

111
00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:41.450
REGEN 10, INSTANT REGEN 4,

112
00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:41.450
DISARM TRAP 5,  DETECT TRAP 4,

113
00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:41.450
DEXTEROUS, ENHANCED REGEN

114
00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:42.500
Wow.

115
00:05:42.580 --> 00:05:43.700
Go forth, Selkan!

116
00:05:45.910 --> 00:05:48.200
Whoa! His skill can disarm traps!

117
00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:50.450
Or not...

118
00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:53.410
He takes the brunt of any traps that cannot be disarmed.

119
00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:55.660
And then regenerates instantly.

120
00:05:57.290 --> 00:06:00.160
Hot damn. That almost feels like cheating.

121
00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:03.200
Excellent work, Selkan!

122
00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:11.870
We can proceed to the second floor
after defeating the sentry monster in here.

123
00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:13.750
A sentry, huh?

124
00:06:13.910 --> 00:06:15.450
Sounds like it's time for a mini-boss.

125
00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:19.830
Selkan is designed only to deal with traps;
he cannot fight whatsoever.

126
00:06:19.950 --> 00:06:22.080
Okay, then we'll take it from here!

127
00:06:20.250 --> 00:06:22.250
B1F SENTRY

128
00:06:20.250 --> 00:06:22.250
UNDEAD SNAKE

129
00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:22.830
C'mon, Jet!

130
00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:25.910
Alright, let's do this!

131
00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:28.410
Attack spell: Fire Javelin!

132
00:06:29.330 --> 00:06:30.450
I shall lend you my aid.

133
00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:33.080
Nether Magic: Hell Storm!

134
00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:38.830
Tri-Explosion!

135
00:06:48.120 --> 00:06:48.750
Bravo.

136
00:06:49.580 --> 00:06:50.790
That went smoothly.

137
00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:52.250
Yeah, piece of cake!

138
00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:56.290
Uh, you sure zombie meat
won't give you a stomachache?

139
00:06:56.700 --> 00:06:57.910
GRRRRMBL

140
00:06:57.910 --> 00:06:59.580
I'm hungry...

141
00:06:59.580 --> 00:07:01.620
Aw, somebody's got a case of the num-nums.

142
00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:05.620
One helping of my super veggie
mountain curry, coming up!

143
00:07:05.790 --> 00:07:08.040
Gotta get your vitamins and fiber.

144
00:07:08.040 --> 00:07:10.870
Curry ish yummeh even inna dunjeon.

145
00:07:11.450 --> 00:07:14.500
My, my. What an intriguing aroma your food has.

146
00:07:14.870 --> 00:07:15.660
Want some?

147
00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:16.700
You don't mind?

148
00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:18.750
Hmph.

149
00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:25.750
Amazing! I simply cannot get enough!

150
00:07:25.750 --> 00:07:27.830
Curry, you say? What a delicacy!

151
00:07:27.950 --> 00:07:31.200
Yeah! Teacher's curry is the greatest ever!
The best food in the world!

152
00:07:31.870 --> 00:07:33.200
Another helping, my good sir!

153
00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:35.290
That's your third bowl! No fair, Jean!

154
00:07:35.700 --> 00:07:36.910
Gimme more!

155
00:07:37.080 --> 00:07:39.620
Says the catgirl on her fifth bowl.

156
00:07:40.870 --> 00:07:42.580
Our spoons cannot be stopped!

157
00:07:42.790 --> 00:07:44.830
Enough, Jean. You're banned from having any more!

158
00:07:45.040 --> 00:07:46.000
Argh...

159
00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:48.660
Whoa, nelly. There's plenty to go around.

160
00:07:48.830 --> 00:07:50.830
SKY ISLAND DUNGEON

161
00:07:48.830 --> 00:07:50.830
B2F

162
00:07:51.580 --> 00:07:53.080
They should be around here.

163
00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:55.910
Oh, those Mimics you were talking about earlier?

164
00:07:57.000 --> 00:07:59.450
At least one of these should
be the rare Counterfeit species.

165
00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:04.370
The only problem is, they're very likely to use
Fake Identity to hide as a regular Mimic.

166
00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:06.160
That's tricky.

167
00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:09.000
Guess we need to attack them
to tell which is which, huh?

168
00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:11.040
Okay. I got it!

169
00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:12.870
Elemental Blade: Fire!

170
00:08:13.500 --> 00:08:15.870
Let's slice and dice these little ghoulies to bits!

171
00:08:19.700 --> 00:08:22.660
September 10th, 3616.

172
00:08:22.910 --> 00:08:26.620
They lopped my right arm off,
so I couldn't write much of anything for awhile.

173
00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:29.830
My writing looks ugly since
I'm not used to using this hand.

174
00:08:30.250 --> 00:08:33.250
But I suppose that nobody will ever read this, anyways.

175
00:08:34.910 --> 00:08:38.250
September 11th, 3616.

176
00:08:38.910 --> 00:08:40.870
I've noticed there are fewer kids around here.

177
00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:44.450
But, luckily, I was able to reunite with my two friends.

178
00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:47.500
The boy's right eye had been gouged out.

179
00:08:47.830 --> 00:08:50.910
And the girl had wounds all over her body.

180
00:08:52.160 --> 00:08:55.910
It makes me so angry.
What did we ever do to deserve this?

181
00:08:57.450 --> 00:09:01.330
September 17th, 3616.

182
00:09:01.910 --> 00:09:05.830
It has been oddly quiet today.
Were there just no experiments or what?

183
00:09:06.660 --> 00:09:09.870
Ah, I wish I could see my two friends.

184
00:09:11.330 --> 00:09:13.000
September 18th.

185
00:09:13.540 --> 00:09:19.290
After experimenting on me, they wanted to see how
much would regenerate, and cut off both my legs.

186
00:09:20.410 --> 00:09:25.790
From what I gather, this laboratory
is for turning living humans into undead monsters.

187
00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:28.330
September 20th.

188
00:09:28.830 --> 00:09:32.200
They're apparently going to infuse me
with animus while I'm still alive.

189
00:09:33.250 --> 00:09:36.500
Are these the pained feelings
of all the kids who died here?

190
00:09:37.500 --> 00:09:41.700
I bet none of them are left.
The animus of my two friends must be part of all this.

191
00:09:43.160 --> 00:09:47.450
Ah, it won't be long now. I feel myself fading away...

192
00:09:53.200 --> 00:09:56.700
That was the day I ceased being human.

193
00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:04.040
Yahoo!

194
00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:06.450
The Fake Identity skill is ours, baby!

195
00:10:06.450 --> 00:10:07.450
Woo!

196
00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:10.450
Bravo. That didn't take you very long at all.

197
00:10:11.160 --> 00:10:12.910
Alright, Fake Identity is now active.

198
00:10:12.910 --> 00:10:15.290
Hey, Jean! Use your Soulsight to look at me!

199
00:10:17.580 --> 00:10:20.160
It works. Your stats appear quite low
and I can see no skills.

200
00:10:20.540 --> 00:10:21.450
Sweet!

201
00:10:21.700 --> 00:10:24.580
However, having no skills whatsoever
is too much of a tip-off.

202
00:10:25.040 --> 00:10:27.290
You should set a few innocuous
ones to make it convincing.

203
00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:28.950
Oh, good call!

204
00:10:29.870 --> 00:10:32.200
We have no further business here on the second floor.

205
00:10:32.370 --> 00:10:34.620
Fran, bring Summon Sphere #2 out of storage.

206
00:10:34.910 --> 00:10:35.620
Roger!

207
00:10:36.080 --> 00:10:38.790
Instant Summon! High Undead!

208
00:10:39.450 --> 00:10:40.830
Come forth, Fly!

209
00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:45.080
FLY

210
00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:45.080
RACE: UNDEAD MONSTER

211
00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:45.080
STATUS: CONTRACT, UNDEAD

212
00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:45.080
VIT:

213
00:10:43.420 --> 00:10:45.080
INT:

214
00:10:43.420 --> 00:10:45.080
STR:

215
00:10:43.420 --> 00:10:45.080
AGI:

216
00:10:43.420 --> 00:10:45.080
SKILLS:

217
00:10:43.420 --> 00:10:45.080
FADE 7, CARTOGRAPHY 6,

218
00:10:43.420 --> 00:10:45.080
COMMUNICATION 3, SHADOW CLONE 7, MANA DRAIN 6,

219
00:10:43.420 --> 00:10:45.080
DETECT TRAP 3, PHYSICAL IMMUNITY

220
00:10:45.870 --> 00:10:47.120
Whoa, it multiplied!

221
00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:48.500
Say hello to my scout.

222
00:10:48.750 --> 00:10:52.450
It's an undead monster I fitted
with a cartography skill to map out dungeons.

223
00:10:52.580 --> 00:10:57.290
That information is then transmitted directly
into my ghastly gray brain.

224
00:10:57.290 --> 00:10:58.870
Your own personal mapmaker, huh?

225
00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:00.910
Man, necromancy really comes in clutch.

226
00:11:01.750 --> 00:11:06.830
Fly and Selkan are an ideal team.
They make the task of dungeon crawling all too easy!

227
00:11:06.830 --> 00:11:09.160
Wow, you're so smart!

228
00:11:10.540 --> 00:11:12.660
By all means, keep the compliments coming!

229
00:11:15.250 --> 00:11:18.330
And so, with Fly and Selkan in the lead...

230
00:11:20.250 --> 00:11:26.870
...traps posed no threat as we zipped through the
complex maze of the dungeon without ever getting lost.

231
00:11:22.700 --> 00:11:23.660
B2F SENTRY:

232
00:11:22.700 --> 00:11:23.660
ZOMBIE OGRE

233
00:11:25.660 --> 00:11:26.870
Flare Blast!

234
00:11:33.250 --> 00:11:37.000
The crystal meter has maxed out
and your abilities have evolved.

235
00:11:37.370 --> 00:11:39.330
Oh, System Lady!

236
00:11:39.750 --> 00:11:42.290
You have acquired 50 Evolution Points.

237
00:11:42.750 --> 00:11:44.870
Hell yeah, it's been a hot minute since my last evolution!

238
00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:47.450
"Evolution"? What is that, exactly?

239
00:11:47.450 --> 00:11:51.500
Uh, well, it's kind of like my unique way of leveling up.

240
00:11:51.660 --> 00:11:52.450
Oh?

241
00:11:53.250 --> 00:11:57.160
You have reached the necessary level
to unlock a new skill: Transform.

242
00:11:55.040 --> 00:11:57.370
NEW SKILL:

243
00:11:55.040 --> 00:11:57.370
TRANSFORM

244
00:11:57.370 --> 00:11:59.500
Wahoo! I love me some new skills!

245
00:11:59.500 --> 00:12:04.040
Transform: This skill enables you to take on
different forms at the cost of MP.

246
00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:06.160
However, it cannot change your mass.

247
00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:08.660
Wow! A Teacher Hammer!

248
00:12:08.910 --> 00:12:12.700
Oof, not my favorite. This skill eats up way too much MP.

249
00:12:12.700 --> 00:12:14.910
We won't be able to use it for very long.

250
00:12:16.910 --> 00:12:19.910
SKY ISLAND DUNGEON

251
00:12:16.910 --> 00:12:19.910
B3F

252
00:12:18.160 --> 00:12:19.330
I am perturbed.

253
00:12:20.160 --> 00:12:20.950
Huh?

254
00:12:21.040 --> 00:12:22.290
What's the matter?

255
00:12:22.750 --> 00:12:24.790
There is a lack of undead monsters down here.

256
00:12:25.160 --> 00:12:27.660
And I keep seeing the remains of ones
that we never fought.

257
00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:31.160
Maybe a case of friendly fire? No, wait...

258
00:12:31.450 --> 00:12:33.080
Hey! Are you thinking what I'm thinking?

259
00:12:33.370 --> 00:12:35.450
Yes, it may be my old foe.

260
00:12:35.870 --> 00:12:36.790
Old foe?

261
00:12:39.250 --> 00:12:40.370
Something's coming this way.

262
00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:49.580
Found you!

263
00:12:50.040 --> 00:12:51.750
Hey, Jean! Is this the one?

264
00:12:55.330 --> 00:12:57.120
Yes, the Undead Eater!

265
00:13:00.950 --> 00:13:03.410
Found you, found you!

266
00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:05.120
Identify.

267
00:13:07.500 --> 00:13:08.830
It has Identify Jammer?!

268
00:13:11.500 --> 00:13:12.290
Bring it on!

269
00:13:12.500 --> 00:13:13.370
Wait, Fran!

270
00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:15.870
I missed!

271
00:13:15.870 --> 00:13:16.830
Look out, Jean!

272
00:13:17.450 --> 00:13:18.250
Go, Jet!

273
00:13:21.370 --> 00:13:23.160
My master!

274
00:13:23.450 --> 00:13:25.120
We finally reunite!

275
00:13:27.580 --> 00:13:31.200
You're not the Undead Eater? Is that you, Stephan?

276
00:13:31.450 --> 00:13:35.250
Yes, it's me! Your loyal minion!

277
00:13:35.700 --> 00:13:36.830
Stephan?

278
00:13:37.500 --> 00:13:38.410
Whozzat?

279
00:13:39.080 --> 00:13:43.040
I left behind a minion for the Undead Eater to feed upon
when I fled the dungeon last time.

280
00:13:43.040 --> 00:13:44.000
Stephan was that minion.

281
00:13:44.000 --> 00:13:45.540
Oh, right. You did mention that.

282
00:13:45.830 --> 00:13:46.870
It's news to me.

283
00:13:47.200 --> 00:13:48.830
Well, yeah, you feel asleep during his story.

284
00:13:49.540 --> 00:13:51.450
I designed Stephan with the following skills:

285
00:13:49.700 --> 00:13:55.620
MASTER~

286
00:13:51.700 --> 00:13:55.950
Undead Resistance, Drain Resistance,
and Erosive Fusion.

287
00:13:56.500 --> 00:13:59.660
The idea was for him to resist
being absorbed by the Undead Eater,

288
00:13:59.830 --> 00:14:01.830
and take it over with Erosive Fusion instead.

289
00:14:02.660 --> 00:14:04.660
But I thought my plan had failed.

290
00:14:04.870 --> 00:14:07.450
It took a few years, but I pulled it off!

291
00:14:07.910 --> 00:14:10.200
Well, I'm sorry I wasn't there for you.

292
00:14:10.450 --> 00:14:11.950
You've made me proud, Stephan!

293
00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:13.080
Thanks.

294
00:14:13.790 --> 00:14:19.200
As I recall it, the Undead Eater was a gargantuan fiend.
Yet you're quite small.

295
00:14:19.700 --> 00:14:23.870
Yeah. It turns out this body can take on different forms.

296
00:14:24.080 --> 00:14:26.620
Since I found it difficult to move at such a huge size,

297
00:14:26.620 --> 00:14:29.830
I tapped into this form that was left behind
in a stream of consciousness.

298
00:14:30.330 --> 00:14:32.580
Or maybe they're someone's memories?

299
00:14:33.160 --> 00:14:35.120
Anyway, that's why I look like this.

300
00:14:36.370 --> 00:14:37.830
Good golly gosh...

301
00:14:40.200 --> 00:14:43.580
I'm so glad to see you again after all this time, Master.

302
00:14:43.580 --> 00:14:45.700
You're just as handsome as I remember!

303
00:14:45.700 --> 00:14:47.870
I could look at you all day!

304
00:14:48.370 --> 00:14:49.620
O-oh really?

305
00:14:50.080 --> 00:14:52.040
That's great! It's nice somebody noticed!

306
00:14:52.040 --> 00:14:53.370
I work hard on my look!

307
00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:57.700
Truly, the greatest necromancer of our time!
You're killing it, sir!

308
00:14:58.160 --> 00:15:00.200
They are totally in their own little world.

309
00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:05.200
By the way, I've been meaning to ask,
are you one of Master Jean's new servants?

310
00:15:05.660 --> 00:15:06.660
Like hell.

311
00:15:09.080 --> 00:15:10.500
Please accept my apologies!

312
00:15:10.500 --> 00:15:13.790
I had no idea that you were
a brave adventurer helping my master out.

313
00:15:13.790 --> 00:15:15.750
It's okay. My name's Fran.

314
00:15:15.750 --> 00:15:18.410
This sword is Teacher and the big boy is Jet.

315
00:15:20.120 --> 00:15:21.250
Well, I'm Stephan!

316
00:15:21.370 --> 00:15:22.660
Nice to meetcha.

317
00:15:22.870 --> 00:15:24.870
SKY ISLAND DUNGEON

318
00:15:22.870 --> 00:15:24.870
B4F

319
00:15:25.410 --> 00:15:32.330
With Stephan in our party,
we blazed through the dungeon even faster than before.

320
00:15:32.750 --> 00:15:36.250
SKY ISLAND DUNGEON

321
00:15:32.750 --> 00:15:36.250
B5F

322
00:15:32.830 --> 00:15:35.790
All my years of wandering
the dungeon are coming in handy.

323
00:15:36.330 --> 00:15:38.160
Please let me be your guide!

324
00:15:39.410 --> 00:15:41.750
This bridge is unstable. I'll show you a detour.

325
00:15:42.370 --> 00:15:47.870
Stephan knew how to get past all the dungeon's
toughest spots and even some shortcuts through it.

326
00:15:50.250 --> 00:15:51.620
Have you noticed, Master?

327
00:15:53.620 --> 00:15:54.370
Mm-hmm.

328
00:15:56.540 --> 00:15:58.540
SKY ISLAND DUNGEON

329
00:15:56.540 --> 00:15:58.540
B6F

330
00:15:58.750 --> 00:15:59.870
Hell Blast!

331
00:15:59.870 --> 00:16:01.040
Hell Blaze!

332
00:16:02.750 --> 00:16:03.620
Wow!

333
00:16:03.620 --> 00:16:05.910
You can use necromancy spells, too?

334
00:16:06.080 --> 00:16:06.950
Yeah.

335
00:16:06.950 --> 00:16:10.160
They seem to be skills of the boy
who this body originally belonged to.

336
00:16:10.450 --> 00:16:13.330
Necronanny spells! So cool!

337
00:16:13.660 --> 00:16:15.660
SKY ISLAND DUNGEON

338
00:16:13.660 --> 00:16:15.660
B7F

339
00:16:14.120 --> 00:16:15.040
Flub alert.

340
00:16:25.790 --> 00:16:27.120
Behind you, Fran!

341
00:16:29.580 --> 00:16:30.450
Stephan...

342
00:16:31.160 --> 00:16:32.200
Thank you!

343
00:16:34.540 --> 00:16:35.330
My pleasure.

344
00:16:36.290 --> 00:16:38.370
I commend your efforts, Stephan.

345
00:16:39.080 --> 00:16:40.120
Y'know, Master...

346
00:16:40.330 --> 00:16:41.000
Hm?

347
00:16:42.080 --> 00:16:45.700
It sure is fun to fight in a party like this!

348
00:16:47.160 --> 00:16:48.370
Glad you think so.

349
00:16:49.000 --> 00:16:51.500
SKY ISLAND DUNGEON

350
00:16:49.000 --> 00:16:51.500
B8F

351
00:16:50.410 --> 00:16:51.500
I can't slice these things!

352
00:16:52.330 --> 00:16:53.750
Damn Arch Wraiths...

353
00:16:54.540 --> 00:16:55.910
Please let me deal with them.

354
00:17:04.200 --> 00:17:06.120
Did you just scarf down that whole swarm of wraiths?

355
00:17:06.120 --> 00:17:07.950
They don't call you the Undead Eater for nothing!

356
00:17:08.200 --> 00:17:09.620
You're amazing, Stephan!

357
00:17:09.790 --> 00:17:10.910
You think so?

358
00:17:11.790 --> 00:17:13.700
Nicely done, Stephan.

359
00:17:18.750 --> 00:17:21.410
The sentry of the 8th floor is just beyond this door.

360
00:17:24.160 --> 00:17:28.290
Pardon me, Fran and Teacher.
I'm going to leave the party for a bit.

361
00:17:28.500 --> 00:17:30.000
Huh? You are?

362
00:17:30.450 --> 00:17:33.500
Yeah, I have to go on a secret mission for my master.

363
00:17:33.660 --> 00:17:35.200
Indeed. It's very important.

364
00:17:35.450 --> 00:17:35.910
Right!

365
00:17:36.870 --> 00:17:40.830
Well, that's a bummer.
I wanted us to fight together a little longer.

366
00:17:40.830 --> 00:17:42.540
I feel the same way.

367
00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:48.790
Bye for now, Jet, Teacher, and Fran.
Please keep my master safe.

368
00:17:49.120 --> 00:17:50.620
Okay, you got it.

369
00:17:51.330 --> 00:17:52.450
Just one more thing...

370
00:17:53.040 --> 00:17:54.160
What is it?

371
00:17:54.830 --> 00:17:55.660
Never mind.

372
00:17:58.040 --> 00:17:58.580
Goodbye!

373
00:18:00.120 --> 00:18:01.950
So, what's this secret mission?

374
00:18:02.500 --> 00:18:04.950
Just a backup plan for emergencies.

375
00:18:05.700 --> 00:18:07.950
I'll explain more if my intuition proves correct.

376
00:18:09.370 --> 00:18:11.000
Now, onto the business at hand.

377
00:18:17.750 --> 00:18:20.200
B8F SENTRY

378
00:18:17.750 --> 00:18:20.200
ELDER ZOMBIE

379
00:18:17.750 --> 00:18:20.200
GREATER SPEARER

380
00:18:20.910 --> 00:18:23.290
It's go time! Blast 'em with magic first!

381
00:18:23.290 --> 00:18:24.000
'Kay!

382
00:18:30.040 --> 00:18:32.040
It sliced our spells right outta the damn air!

383
00:18:33.290 --> 00:18:34.200
No problem.

384
00:18:34.580 --> 00:18:35.620
Two can play at that game!

385
00:18:36.120 --> 00:18:37.040
Be careful.

386
00:18:37.410 --> 00:18:38.950
It has an enchanted weapon.

387
00:18:39.540 --> 00:18:41.540
And even the Advanced Spear Mastery skill.

388
00:18:41.950 --> 00:18:43.330
This thing is no joke!

389
00:18:51.120 --> 00:18:52.870
So what? We have Advanced Sword Mastery!

390
00:18:52.870 --> 00:18:54.540
And a super amazing sword!

391
00:19:00.450 --> 00:19:00.870
Jet!

392
00:19:03.330 --> 00:19:04.370
You okay, Fran?

393
00:19:04.620 --> 00:19:07.700
Yeah, the divine protection
of the Black Cat set saved me.

394
00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:11.540
I must say, this sentry is
a cut far above any of the others!

395
00:19:12.290 --> 00:19:13.040
Jet!

396
00:19:14.410 --> 00:19:15.830
Air Leap!

397
00:19:24.410 --> 00:19:26.870
Damn, not even Fran's swordplay can trip this thing up?

398
00:19:27.620 --> 00:19:29.950
Watch out, Fran! It's charging up mana!

399
00:19:34.910 --> 00:19:35.870
Yikes, close one!

400
00:19:36.450 --> 00:19:38.040
That spear is annoying.

401
00:19:38.200 --> 00:19:38.950
You said it.

402
00:19:39.250 --> 00:19:41.540
Let's focus on attacking the spear until it breaks!

403
00:19:41.540 --> 00:19:43.450
I was thinking the same thing.

404
00:19:43.540 --> 00:19:44.540
Great.

405
00:19:44.870 --> 00:19:47.080
I'll throw an amplified spell right in its face.

406
00:19:47.330 --> 00:19:49.160
You aim to strike the same spot, okay?

407
00:19:49.160 --> 00:19:50.540
'Kay. I'm ready!

408
00:19:50.750 --> 00:19:51.870
Split Mind!

409
00:19:52.450 --> 00:19:54.790
Amplify to the max...

410
00:19:55.290 --> 00:19:57.000
Explosion!

411
00:20:03.700 --> 00:20:04.540
We're not done yet!

412
00:20:04.750 --> 00:20:05.790
Have another one!

413
00:20:07.950 --> 00:20:09.750
Now's our chance, Fran! You know what to do!

414
00:20:09.750 --> 00:20:10.540
Right!

415
00:20:11.160 --> 00:20:12.120
Advanced Sword Art...

416
00:20:13.080 --> 00:20:15.200
Impact Slash!

417
00:20:25.700 --> 00:20:27.250
Crystal absorbed.

418
00:20:28.080 --> 00:20:29.620
Whew, we won!

419
00:20:29.870 --> 00:20:31.660
You were incredible, Fran.

420
00:20:33.370 --> 00:20:37.910
Marvelous, simply marvelous!
You made short work of a very formidable zombie.

421
00:20:38.250 --> 00:20:40.700
Our odds were bound to get worse
the longer the fight went on.

422
00:20:41.000 --> 00:20:43.330
So we had to pull out all the stops right away.

423
00:20:43.870 --> 00:20:46.040
That last attack was quite ferocious.

424
00:20:46.580 --> 00:20:50.950
Impact Slash. It's the most powerful move
in Fran's arsenal right now.

425
00:20:52.370 --> 00:20:54.790
We would've been in trouble
if that attack wasn't enough to win.

426
00:20:56.160 --> 00:20:58.660
Teacher can make sound decisions
in the heat of the moment,

427
00:20:58.870 --> 00:21:01.910
while Fran has the adaptivity to respond to them quickly.

428
00:21:01.910 --> 00:21:03.660
You truly are an incredible team.

429
00:21:03.870 --> 00:21:04.500
Yep.

430
00:21:05.120 --> 00:21:07.870
Teacher and I are the perfect pair!

431
00:21:08.120 --> 00:21:09.870
We're golden!

432
00:21:11.250 --> 00:21:14.870
But I must say, that sentry was oddly strong
to be on the 8th floor.

433
00:21:14.870 --> 00:21:17.290
Especially considering there are
10 floors in this dungeon.

434
00:21:17.910 --> 00:21:20.370
Fran. Make sure to recover back to full health.

435
00:21:20.370 --> 00:21:22.370
Right. The real fight is yet to come.

436
00:21:24.540 --> 00:21:27.040
SKY ISLAND DUNGEON

437
00:21:24.540 --> 00:21:27.040
B9F FINAL AREA

438
00:21:26.000 --> 00:21:29.080
Well, this is the last hurdle.

439
00:21:29.290 --> 00:21:31.830
The only thing after this room
is the dungeon core chamber.

440
00:21:35.040 --> 00:21:36.870
There's the 9th floor sentry.

441
00:21:37.370 --> 00:21:40.160
Let's get cracking! Hit it with a full barrage!

442
00:21:50.160 --> 00:21:51.410
Finally.

443
00:21:53.500 --> 00:21:56.000
We've been looking for you, bonehead.

444
00:21:57.910 --> 00:21:59.620
It's time for some payback.

445
00:22:00.290 --> 00:22:01.160
You're going down!

446
00:23:33.950 --> 00:23:39.950
NEXT EPISODE:

447
00:23:33.950 --> 00:23:39.950
THE UNDEAD MONSTER WAS TOUGH AS NAILS

